    <solution><m>\bf r\it'(t)=\frac{\,d}{\,dt}\left\lt e^t,e^{7 t},-8\right&gt;=\left\lt e^t,7 e^{7 t},0\right&gt;</m>



<m>g'(t)=\frac{\,d}{\,dt}\left(7 t - 2\right)=7</m>



Using the Chain Rule we get:



<m>\frac{\,d}{\,dt}\bf r\it(g(t))=g'(t) \bf r\it'(g(t))=7\left\lt e^{7 t - 2},7 e^{7\left(7 t - 2\right)},0\right&gt;=\left\lt 7 e^{7 t - 2}, 49 e^{7\left(7 t - 2\right)},0\right&gt;</m>



</solution>
